// Test: bugfixes/codegen_body_local_call_alloc_leak_in_loop
// Grammar: while_statement, variable_declaration, assignment,
//          class_declaration, method_call, constructor_call
// Semantic: SEM020 (accumulator pattern), heap-scope invariant
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.154
//
// Regression target: SSR-STRING-CONCAT-LOOP-OOM-33151 (#8c113611781e),
// revised leak class documented in
// codegen-body-local-alloc-leak-in-accum-loop (#69a07166cc59), discovered
// after commit a4a6ecd2 (v0.33.153).
//
// a4a6ecd2 wrapped call fragments in `acc = acc + <call>` self-appends
// with per-call scope_push/scope_pop_keeping. It did NOT cover
// loop-body-LOCAL declarations whose initializer is an allocating call —
// including constructors and methods that return strings.
//
// The failing shape (condensed from Companion.buildCategorySections):
//
//     while catJson != ""
//         RenderSyntaxCategorySection sec = RenderSyntaxCategorySection(catJson)
//         acc = acc + sec.serve()
//         i = i + 1
//         catJson = json.get(categoriesJson, i.toString())
//
// `catJson` is covered by the carryover pass (declared outside the loop,
// single reassign inside). `acc` is covered by the accumulator rewrite
// with per-call wrapping of `sec.serve()`. But `sec` is declared INSIDE
// the loop body, its RHS (a constructor call) allocates class-instance
// state on the main heap every iteration, and NOTHING reclaims those
// allocations until the outer mem_scope_mark pops at end-of-loop.
//
// The 0.33.154 fix is a new HIR post-pass
// (`hoist_scope_push_above_body_local_alloc_decls` in
// `src/hir/hir_builder.rs`) that detects, right after
// `rewrite_self_append_in_block`, the sequence
//
//   VarDecl D:<non-string> = <allocating call>            (body-local)
//   VarDecl __sb_N_ppmark_K:Integer = scope_push()
//   VarDecl __sb_N_ptmp_K:String   = <expr reading D>
//   Assign  __sb_N_ptmp_K = scope_pop_keeping(mark, tmp)
//   Assign  __sb_N        = string_builder_append(__sb_N, tmp)
//
// and swaps D with the mark decl when D is not read outside the group
// and doesn't escape. That puts D's allocation ABOVE the mark, so the
// existing scope_pop_keeping reclaims the shell every iter alongside
// the intermediates it was already reclaiming.
//
// This test reproduces the leak class in isolation: a body-local class
// instance whose constructor holds a per-iter string field, at an
// iteration count that traps v0.33.153 (which crashed at ~40k iters
// with any Payload shape). At 40000 iters, expected length is
// 40000 * len("row;") = 160000.
//
// Expected output:
//   160000

start:
	string acc = ""
	integer i = 0
	string seed = "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
	integer iters = 40000
	while i < iters
		Payload p = Payload(seed)
		acc = acc + p.tag()
		i = i + 1
	printl(acc.length().toString())

class Payload
	string body

	constructor(string seed)
		body = seed

	functions:
		public:
			string tag()
				return "row;"
